    <item>
      <title>code-modernization: an uplift is not proven by a typed baseline or edited tests</title>
      <link>https://github.com/anthropics/claude-plugins-official/commit/f45794fa4831636e7ae55f8081769c8ebf3f58c6</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">f45794f</guid>
      <pubDate>Fri, 25 Sep 2026 04:18:46 GMT</pubDate>
      <category>gh-commits-plugins-official</category>
      <description>Three ways a same-technology uplift could come out PROVEN too easily:  - The baseline came from a table someone typed. It now counts as measured   only when the script can read per-test results (JUnit or TRX XML, a runner   log with a summary line, or per-test JSON) from analysis/&lt;system&gt;/baseline/ </description>
    </item>
